Sure! Below is a minimal example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML & CSS (no JavaScript).  
When you hover over the card, it smoothly rotates around its center.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container ----------
   Keeps the card centered on the page */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;          /* full viewport height */
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* ---------- Card ----------
   Basic styling + perspective for 3D effect */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective:800px;     /* gives depth to the rotation */
}
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* allows children to be positioned in 3D space */
    transition:transform .6s ease; /* smooth animation */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y‑axis */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- Front & Back Faces ----------
   Positioned absolutely so they overlap each other */
.front,
.back {
    position:absolute;
    top:0;
    left:0;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden; /* hide backside during rotation */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    color:white;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    padding:20px;
    box-sizing:border-box;
}

.front {background:#3498db;}
.back  {background:#e74c3c; transform:rotateY(180deg);} /* rotated so it shows after flip */

/* Optional: add some text styling */
h2 {margin:0 0 10px;}
p {margin:0; line-height:1.5;}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front Face -->
        <div class="front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>This is the front side of the card.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back Face -->
        <div class="back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>And this is the back side.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a `perspective` so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both faces, has `transform-style: preserve-3d` and a transition for smoothness. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each face is absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the reverse side while rotating. |
| `.back` | Rotated 180° initially so that when the parent flips, it becomes visible. |

Feel free to replace the colors, content, or dimensions with your own design. Happy coding!
